<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Hamant et al. (2008) & Uyttewaal et al. (2012) shoot apical meristem pressurized shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, and katanin organ boundary morphogenesis (Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells))",
        "Bozorg et al. (2014), Sampathkumar et al. (2014), Hamant et al. (2008) & Uyttewaal et al. (2012) shoot apical meristem pressurized shell stress tensor, stress-vs-strain CMT alignment, and katanin organ boundary morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 93.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py> ;
    schema:about "Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular molecular dynamics of individual katanin hexamer ATP hydrolysis or full 3D internal L2/L3 corpus cell division genealogy",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D/3D finite-element / continuum shell turgor stress and anisotropic viscoplastic Lockhart growth solver across all 4 canonical SAM zones (Central Dome K>0, Peripheral Flank, Organ-Meristem Saddle Boundary K<0, and Cylindrical Stem sigma_theta/sigma_z = 2.0), verifying Law 1 saddle stress amplification (residual 0.0), Law 2 2:1 cylindrical Laplace switch and longitudinal elongation, and Law 3 katanin/oryzalin stiffness anisotropy reduction (residual 0.0)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Bozorg et al. (2014) stress-vs-strain directional cue discrimination (stress cue r = 0.9910 vs strain cue control r = -0.4150), 24-cell Kirsch single-cell laser ablation ring reorientation (<cos^2> = 0.8997 vs strain control 0.3512), 5-condition perturbation sweep (Pearson r = 0.9992, p = 2.41e-5, RMSE = 0.3125 um), and Sobel/Gaussian structure-tensor segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana SAM histology section (`arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg`, 1200x800 px)",
        "reported_in_source: Bozorg, Krupinski & Jönsson (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 and Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 pressurized shell and finite-element stress model demonstrating isotropic stress on the central SAM dome (K > 0), highly anisotropic tensile stress along the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ-meristem saddle boundary (K = kappa_1 * kappa_2 < 0), 2:1 circumferential-to-axial Laplace stress on the cylindrical stem driving longitudinal Lockhart elongation, and stress-cue (not strain-cue) reproduction of circumferential microtubule alignment around single-cell laser ablations",
        "reported_in_source: Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 and Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 demonstrating that katanin (BOT1/KTN1) severing controls mechanical feedback gain gamma_MT and that bot1/ktn1 mutation or oryzalin microtubule depolymerization reduces CMT ordering and flattens the organ boundary crease",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D/3D continuum and vertex shell mechanics of the L1 epidermal tunica coupled to orthotropic cellulose microfibril reinforcement and 2D histological structure-tensor morphometrics" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/2008-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem.py; output: docs/media/microtubule_stress_meristem_comparison.png; organism: Arabidopsis thaliana (shoot apical meristem L1 epidermal shell, organ-meristem saddle boundary, cylindrical stem, and epidermal cells); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 58c04b2b1d6826f3891b148876d3e11ab4e8c9ee2c8ea4cca35459f9bbf26dca; artifact_sha256: daf51bf0d63a2152304a1685871e8db5e6a1aae1f66e1fd1e2823e3c9efbacbc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg=3a8b54b71f7c780c..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/microtubule_stress_meristem_reference.json=3e04a6dded528819..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/paper_citations.bib=9355fa7c7b784918..., datasets/microtubule_stress_meristem/scout_manifest.json=e3cd62cc5263f317...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bozorg, Krupinski & Jönsson (2014) PLoS Comput. Biol. 10(1):e1003410 and Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 pressurized shell and finite-element stress model demonstrating isotropic stress on the central SAM dome (K > 0), highly anisotropic tensile stress along the negative-Gaussian-curvature organ-meristem saddle boundary (K = kappa_1 * kappa_2 < 0), 2:1 circumferential-to-axial Laplace stress on the cylindrical stem driving longitudinal Lockhart elongation, and stress-cue (not strain-cue) reproduction of circumferential microtubule alignment around single-cell laser ablations | Uyttewaal et al. (2012) Cell 149:439-451 and Sampathkumar et al. (2014) eLife 3:e01967 demonstrating that katanin (BOT1/KTN1) severing controls mechanical feedback gain gamma_MT and that bot1/ktn1 mutation or oryzalin microtubule depolymerization reduces CMT ordering and flattens the organ boundary crease; reconstructed_in_script: 2D/3D finite-element / continuum shell turgor stress and anisotropic viscoplastic Lockhart growth solver across all 4 canonical SAM zones (Central Dome K>0, Peripheral Flank, Organ-Meristem Saddle Boundary K<0, and Cylindrical Stem sigma_theta/sigma_z = 2.0), verifying Law 1 saddle stress amplification (residual 0.0), Law 2 2:1 cylindrical Laplace switch and longitudinal elongation, and Law 3 katanin/oryzalin stiffness anisotropy reduction (residual 0.0) | Bozorg et al. (2014) stress-vs-strain directional cue discrimination (stress cue r = 0.9910 vs strain cue control r = -0.4150), 24-cell Kirsch single-cell laser ablation ring reorientation (<cos^2> = 0.8997 vs strain control 0.3512), 5-condition perturbation sweep (Pearson r = 0.9992, p = 2.41e-5, RMSE = 0.3125 um), and Sobel/Gaussian structure-tensor segmentation of the SHA-256-locked Arabidopsis thaliana SAM histology section (`arabidopsis_meristem_boundary_specimen.jpg`, 1200x800 px); transfer_boundary: 2D/3D continuum and vertex shell mechanics of the L1 epidermal tunica coupled to orthotropic cellulose microfibril reinforcement and 2D histological structure-tensor morphometrics; does_not_claim: Subcellular molecular dynamics of individual katanin hexamer ATP hydrolysis or full 3D internal L2/L3 corpus cell division genealogy]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2012.02.048>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1003410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.01967> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-microtubule-stress-meristem-audit-v2-hamant-microtubule-stress-meristem-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Finite-Element Pressurized Shell Turgor Stress Tensor, Bozorg Stress-vs-Strain Cue Discrimination & Anisotropic Viscoplastic Lockhart Growth" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 9.33e-01 .

